{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112100,"nonce":"C6cAScgDhzzOzklipuoQaIuHvmM=","title":"0.1 Spike: agent profile, headless boot, tick throughput","message":"Wave 0 — feasibility. Depends: nothing. Gates: every other wave.\n\n## Goal\nRetire the platform's empirical unknowns and produce FINDINGS.md whose\nconclusions amend the wave 1-3 specs before they are implemented.\n\n## Context (read first)\n- DESIGN.md (all of it; esp. Bench, Time model, Non-goals)\n- `_RimWorld-Test/make-profile.sh` — the symlink-farm bench pattern to copy\n- `_RimWorld-Testing/run-testing.sh` — isolation (XDG_CONFIG_HOME, Steam\n  detach) + mangohud fps-cap pattern\n- decompiled `TickManager.cs` (TickManagerUpdate budget, TickRateMultiplier,\n  UltraSpeedBoost), `Root_Play.cs:85` SetupForQuickTestPlay (newgame recipe)\n- Zetrith's Multiplayer source (fetch/locate) — its catch-up/fast-forward loop\n  is the authority on which per-frame updates a tick-loop must preserve\n\n## Tasks\n1. `profile/make-profile-agent.sh` building `../_RimWorld-Agent` with the v1\n   mod set from DESIGN.md §Bench. Resolve transitive deps of Hospitality/\n   Gastronomy/Storefront (HugsLib etc.) from their About.xml at build time.\n   Verify SeekAndKill actually loads+functions without PerspectiveShift (its\n   About declares only Harmony; if it no-ops without PS, add PS + note it).\n   `run-agent.sh` with full isolation; window to Hyprland special workspace\n   via windowrule (silent, no focus steal); fps cap configurable.\n2. Boot to main menu, then into a generated map. Zero red errors required\n   (mod-load warnings triaged in FINDINGS.md).\n3. `-batchmode -nographics` experiment: attempt boot→load→tick. Record outcome\n   either way; nothing depends on success.\n4. Throughput: on a small test colony measure sustained tps at Fast/Ultrafast/\n   UltraSpeedBoost AND via a throwaway GameComponent driving a budgeted\n   DoSingleTick loop. Record thermal behavior (temps, fan) over ≥10min\n   sustained; recommend the default max_tps cap.\n5. Enumerate the per-frame update set a fast-forward loop must run (from MP's\n   catch-up code + empirical checks: power nets, lords, weather).\n6. Confirm Xvfb fallback boots (document; don't polish).\n\n## Invariants\nNEVER launch `_RimWorld-Testing` or the MP install. No Steam attach. This\nissue is the only one allowed to leave scratch experiments uncommitted; the\nprofile scripts + FINDINGS.md are the deliverables.\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nProfile script layout/flags; whether UltraSpeedBoost is reachable\nprogrammatically outside dev mode; default fps caps watched/unwatched.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `_RimWorld-Agent` boots to a playable map with the full v1 modlist, zero red\n  errors in Player.log.\n- Both display modes demonstrated (special workspace + Xvfb), script-flagged.\n- FINDINGS.md committed: tps table, thermal notes + recommended cap, per-frame\n  update set, batchmode verdict, modlist deviations (PS? HugsLib?).","files":null}]}